{
 "help": "usage: wgsextract lineage mt-haplogroup [-h] [--download | --no-download]\n                                        [--tree {phylotree-fu-rcrs,phylotree-rcrs,mitotree-rcrs}]\n                                        [--contamination] [--haplogrep-path HAPLOGREP_PATH]\n                                        [--haplocheck-path HAPLOCHECK_PATH] [--tree-links]\n                                        [--help-all]\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --download, --no-download\n                        Allow missing public reference/model downloads; no sample files or\n                        genotypes are uploaded. Hosts and request data: docs/privacy.md. Default:\n                        config allow_reference_downloads, else off.\n  --tree {phylotree-fu-rcrs,phylotree-rcrs,mitotree-rcrs}\n                        Haplogrep 3 tree (default: config haplogrep_tree, else phylotree-fu-rcrs,\n                        PhyloTree 17 Forensic Update). phylotree-rcrs is PhyloTree 17; mitotree-\n                        rcrs is FamilyTreeDNA Mitotree (non-commercial use only).\n  --contamination       Also check for mtDNA contamination with haplocheck; a BAM/CRAM also keeps\n                        mutserve's heteroplasmy calls for `report`. VCF input needs heteroplasmy\n                        levels (FORMAT/AF).\n  --haplogrep-path HAPLOGREP_PATH\n                        Path to the Haplogrep 3 executable or JAR (optional if in PATH)\n  --haplocheck-path HAPLOCHECK_PATH\n                        Path to the haplocheck executable or JAR (optional if in PATH)\n  --tree-links          Print YFull and FamilyTreeDNA mtDNA tree links.\n  --help-all            Show this help with the advanced options too, and exit.\n\nglobal options:\n  -i/--input, -o/--outdir, --genome, --ref, -t/--threads, -m/--memory, --json, --quiet, --debug,\n  --config and the other global options are accepted before or after the command; 'wgsextract\n  --help' lists them all.\n\n1 advanced option not shown; 'wgsextract lineage mt-haplogroup --help-all' lists them.\n\nexamples:\n  wgsextract lineage mt-haplogroup --input sample.cram\n  wgsextract lineage mt-haplogroup --input sample.cram --contamination\n  wgsextract lineage mt-haplogroup --input sample.vcf.gz --tree mitotree-rcrs\n\noutputs (in the output directory unless noted):\n  haplogrep_results.txt; prints the mtDNA haplogroup and Haplogrep 3 tree.\n  With --contamination, also haplocheck_contamination.txt (+ .raw.txt, .html).\n\nneeds:\n  bcftools, haplogrep3, java, samtools; depending on options and inputs, also:\n  curl, haplocheck, tabix; minutes on a 30x genome.\n",
